VCP's recorded patches raise the codex-chatgpt crate recursion limit and register
selected Munarium libraries in the shared workspace and lockfile. Further changes
register the local CPU embedding adapter and its reviewed dependencies, followed
by the original local-corpus qualification executable and its retained governance
dependencies. The continuation-admission patch adapts the retained controller,
extension API and turn-input tests to support host denial of delegated starts.
The scoped-lifecycle patch adds controller thread identity, owned retained
interruption and the original lifecycle host workspace/lock entry. The lifecycle
recovery patch adds private startup and dispatch admission, completion receipts,
native job membership observation and existing lifecycle dependencies. Modified
files carry modification notices. See the ordered patch record
under src/third_party/patches/codex/ and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
The storage qualification patch connects the original comparison package to
existing age, Ed25519, SQLite and retained search dependencies. Its public age
test vector and independent qualification tool are attributed in
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

The P1 foundation and accounting patches register original domain, protocol,
store, engine, budget and audit packages in the retained workspace/lockfile.
The P2 context patch registers original repository and context packages with
existing pinned dependencies and retained native process containment.
The P2 provider patch registers original codec/host dependencies and adds a host
deadline to retained HTTP response headers and body without changing external pins.
The P2 prepared-file patch exposes pure exact preparation in the retained Codex
patch engine and registers original native tool dependencies. Original upstream
line-ending and parser behavior is retained for existing callers.
The P2 policy patch registers original authority evaluation and canonical policy
dependencies using the same external dependency pins.
The canonical host patch adapts retained HTTP admission and raw-body capture
to these libraries, using existing dependency identities.

